  "note": "Tally.Raise takes an argument named `count`, the same name as the tally's field, and its given reads `count.value > old.count.value`. The bare name is the argument (C2.2) and `old.count` is the count the tally holds, so with the stored count at 10 a Raise to 12 is accepted, and a Raise to 11 is then refused GivenNotMet against the 12 now held. Read bare on both sides the rule would compare the argument with itself and refuse both.",
